.TH EUCLID-CLI-EQS-RECEIVE-MESSAGES 1 "August 2026" "euclid-cli 1.0.53" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-eqs-receive-messages \- receive messages from a queue
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli eqs receive-messages
.BR \-\-ern | \-e
.I ERN
[\fB\-\-maxCount\fR|\fB\-m\fR \fIN\fR]
[\fB\-\-waitTime\fR|\fB\-w\fR \fISECONDS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Receives messages from a queue. If messages are available, returns up
to
.B \-\-maxCount
messages. The returned messages favor higher priority ones:
.B \-\-maxCount
slots are split across LOW/MIDDLE/HIGH priority proportionally to the
server's configurable priority weights (4:2:1 by default), so most of a
batch is HIGH priority, fewer MIDDLE, and fewer still LOW.
.PP
Each received message becomes invisible to other receivers for its
visibility timeout (set at queue creation, see
.BR euclid-cli-eqs-create-queue (1),
or per-message via
.BR euclid-cli-eqs-set-message-visibility (1)),
until it is deleted or the timeout expires.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-ern " " \fIERN\fR
Euclid resource name of the queue to receive from. Required.
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-maxCount " " \fIN\fR
Maximum number of messages to receive. Defaults to \fI10\fR.
.TP
.BR \-w ", " \-\-waitTime " " \fISECONDS\fR
Maximum time to wait for messages to become available. Defaults to
\fI0\fR (return immediately with whatever is available).
.PP
The queue may be given by
.B name
instead of by ERN, in which case it is resolved in your session's account
and namespace; see
.B NAMES AND ERNS
in
.BR euclid-cli-eqs (1).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The received messages (possibly none) are printed as JSON.
.TP
.B 1
Missing/invalid arguments, the server could not be reached, or no queue
with that ERN exists.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 eqs receive-messages \e
    --ern ern:queues:eu-central-1:000000000000:queue:orders

euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 eqs receive-messages \e
    --ern ern:queues:eu-central-1:000000000000:queue:orders \e
    --maxCount 5 --waitTime 10
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli-eqs (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eqs-send-message (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eqs-list-messages (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eqs-set-message-visibility (1)
